// A static's initializer is held to the rules a run-time bind is: a function of another shape for an `fnptr`, a
// `bool` into a payload's `int32`, an integer for an enum. Each was unreachable while a static could hold only a
// scalar constant, and must not become a silent conversion now that it holds the rest.
fnptr int32 F(int32 x);
fn int32 add(int32 x, int32 y) { return x + y; }
static F f = add;
static Optional<int32> o = Optional::Some(value: true);
fn uint8 main() { return 0; }
